  "proof": [
    "Read-only duplication of the original ticket descriptor preserves the old mm without reopening its numeric TID or upgrading descriptor access.",
    "The actual stopped destination owns a fresh unpublished private mapping; its active alias proves actual image identity and is reclaimed before the requested operation.",
    "Two same-file replacements recreate the original private allocation at the same address with identical bytes. One source scratch is freed before exec. Both guarded unmaps return operation_canceled without a completed value or leftover recovery.",
    "Same-mm cleanup succeeds. Explicit stopped-peer cleanup after the original task SIGKILL removes the old allocation while the actual original mm remains alive.",
    "Every selected GP/extended register, signal mask, program byte and ptrace owner is independently preserved. Replacement maps and bytes remain intact after rejection.",
    "The replacement/peer processes are actually reaped and the controller restores its original process-local subreaper setting."
  ],
  "proofLimits": [
    "Fresh completed-ticket cases use native ELF64; existing full gates retain native i386 coverage but do not prove these new transitions on i386, x32, ARM, Wine or other kernels.",
    "Standalone checkImage is pinned-mm liveness/known-retirement, not fresh stopped-target affinity authorization.",
    "Explicit peer selection/ptrace ownership is provided by the caller. Automatic separate-old-mm peer discovery, service selected-thread-death retained-allocation handoff and general native-frame ownership remain unfinished.",
    "Fresh private proof requires a current-image mmap and writable current proc descriptor; restrictive syscall policies and read-only proof transports still need implementation.",
    "Conflicting dual guards are both checked in code but lack a dedicated new fixture; incomplete/probe-cleanup failures and concurrent exec windows need further live evidence.",
    "The mixed-ABI adapter and broader six-area compatibility goal remain unpublished/incomplete; historical evidence checkpoints have not been rewritten."
  ]
